# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DialogueActs.mgr - Phase 9 item 3.
#
# Neutral-tagged clause templates for the interrogation-corpus dialogue acts
# that Statements.mgr / Questions.mgr / Formulaics.mgr do not already cover.
# Pre-existing coverage:
#   ASK_FACT, ASK_SLOT, ASK_ENUMERATE, ASK_KNOWLEDGE  - Questions.mgr
#   TELL_FACT (most descriptive shapes)               - Statements.mgr
#   GREETING / CLOSING, AFFIRM/DENY (formulaic)       - Formulaics.mgr
#
# This file adds:
#   EXPRESS_EMOTION    - { ?_I /pres emotion [k <kind>] [?focus] }
#   EMPATHIZE          - speaker's emotion ABOUT the listener
#   OBSERVE_AFFECT     - { ?_you /pres emotion [k <kind>] } - inspector names
#                        the listener's apparent state
#   NEGATIVE_KNOWLEDGE - sentinel @unknown with broader surface vocabulary
#   DECLINE            - sentinel @unknown with refusal surface (shares MC
#                        with NEGATIVE_KNOWLEDGE for v1; differentiates once
#                        (refuse-to-answer <reason>) lands as a func)
#
# Acts NOT yet covered and their blockers (distillation 1 / 1a):
#   HEDGE              - "I think" surface prefix on a TELL_FACT. The MC is
#                        the un-hedged belief; the surface "I think" needs a
#                        wrapper at the :MSG level that produces (msg ...).
#                        Defer until belief-confidence-from-hedge plumbing
#                        is designed (the spec ties hedge to salience).
#   ACCUSE / CONFRONT  - need hostile-content predicate labels (lie, deceive,
#                        protect, conceal) in States.mon.
#   THREATEN / PROMISE - future-tense (msg ...) bodies + predicate gap.
#   PRESENT_EVIDENCE   - composite (msg + ASK_KNOWLEDGE); needs the dialogue
#                        session to track the indicated object across turns.
#   REQUEST_ACTION     - needs a new (request <actor> <action>) func.
#   REQUEST_PERMISSION - needs a new (permitted? <actor> <action>) func.
#   ASK_NARRATIVE      - tell_about is the v1 facsimile; proper recount
#                        needs discourse-planner topic anchors.
#   PROBE_FOR_DETAIL   - dialogue-session-state dependent (item 5).
#   SILENT_PROMPT      - turn marker, not a speech act (item 5).
#   TURN_QUESTION_BACK - needs the session's last-ASK_SLOT recorded so the
#                        matcher can auto-flip it (item 5).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

:ST

# === EXPRESS_EMOTION ========================================================
# The speaker reports their own emotion. Mirrors the witness-side third-party
# templates in Statements.mgr but with ?_I as the subject.

# Joy (ambient)
" i am happy "
{ ?_I /pres emotion [k joy ] } .
" i am glad "
{ ?_I /pres emotion [k joy ] } .

# Joy (focused)
" i am happy about $value(NP) "
{ ?_I /pres emotion [k joy ] $value(NP) } .
" i rejoice in $value(NP) "
{ ?_I /pres emotion [k joy ] $value(NP) } .

# Grief (ambient)
" i am sad "
{ ?_I /pres emotion [k grief ] } .
" i grieve "
{ ?_I /pres emotion [k grief ] } .

# Grief (focused)
" i mourn $value(NP) "
{ ?_I /pres emotion [k grief ] $value(NP) } .
" i grieve for $value(NP) "
{ ?_I /pres emotion [k grief ] $value(NP) } .

# Fear (ambient)
" i am afraid "
{ ?_I /pres emotion [k fear ] } .
" i am frightened "
{ ?_I /pres emotion [k fear ] } .

# Fear (focused)
" i fear $value(NP) "
{ ?_I /pres emotion [k fear ] $value(NP) } .
" i am afraid of $value(NP) "
{ ?_I /pres emotion [k fear ] $value(NP) } .

# Anger (ambient)
" i am angry "
{ ?_I /pres emotion [k anger ] } .

# Anger (focused)
" i am angry with $value(NP) "
{ ?_I /pres emotion [k anger ] $value(NP) } .


# === PRESSURE (witness self-disclosure) =====================================
# Pressure beliefs are direction-laden: the aux slot tells us whether the
# speaker is the actor (CONFESSION register) or the patient/witness
# (GRIEVANCE / LAMENT / GRUDGE / FEAR register). These two speech-acts use
# opposite first-person framing - a confession owns the act ("I have
# something on my conscience"); a grievance casts the speaker as patient
# ("X put me out", "X jilted me", "X and I have not had a civil word").
#
# Phrasings draw on Docs/dialogue_witness_interview_vocabulary.md Section U
# (the volunteered-line corpus). The literals are 19th-c English period-
# Jersey; non-LOJ:1897 deployments would re-author per sociolect.
#
# The matcher discriminates by belief structure:
#   - kind literal [k <kind>] in the target slot pins to one pressure kind
#   - ?_I in the aux slot binds only to the speaker's own self-reference
#     (boundary externalises mself -> abs(self) which equals msg_context->I)
#   - $value(NP) in the aux slot binds any third-party reference
# Per-kind direction is fixed by the appraisal taxonomy:
#   moral_violation: self-inflicted (aux always == self)
#   exposure_risk:   self-inflicted underlying; aux is the potential exposer
#   humiliation / injustice / attachment_loss / rivalry_pressure:
#     other-inflicted (aux is the actor/perpetrator/rival/lost-one)
#
# Tier-gated by inject_pressure_discharge_beliefs via
# pressure_disclosable_at_tier (disclosure_bands.cc): intimate-only for
# moral_violation / exposure_risk; friend for the personal grievances;
# acquaintance for rivalry_pressure.

# --- moral_violation (self-inflicted; aux == self) - CONFESSION
" i have something on my conscience, sir "
{ ?_I /pres pressure [k moral_violation ] ?_I } .

" i have carried something on my conscience and i cannot carry it another day "
{ ?_I /pres pressure [k moral_violation ] ?_I } .
:: flowery

" my conscience troubles me "
{ ?_I /pres pressure [k moral_violation ] ?_I } .
:: curt

# --- exposure_risk (self-inflicted underlying act; aux = potential exposer) - FEAR
" if $value(NP) learns of it, sir, i am done "
{ ?_I /pres pressure [k exposure_risk ] $value(NP) } .

" i live in dread of what $value(NP) may say "
{ ?_I /pres pressure [k exposure_risk ] $value(NP) } .
:: flowery

" $value(NP) could ruin me "
{ ?_I /pres pressure [k exposure_risk ] $value(NP) } .
:: curt

# --- humiliation (other-inflicted; aux = perpetrator) - GRIEVANCE
" $value(NP) shamed me, sir "
{ ?_I /pres pressure [k humiliation ] $value(NP) } .

" i have not forgotten the humiliation $value(NP) dealt me "
{ ?_I /pres pressure [k humiliation ] $value(NP) } .
:: flowery

" $value(NP) put me out "
{ ?_I /pres pressure [k humiliation ] $value(NP) } .
:: curt

# --- injustice (other-inflicted; aux = perpetrator) - GRIEVANCE
" $value(NP) wronged me, sir "
{ ?_I /pres pressure [k injustice ] $value(NP) } .

" there was a wrong $value(NP) did, sir, which i have carried ever since "
{ ?_I /pres pressure [k injustice ] $value(NP) } .
:: flowery

" $value(NP) - a wrong, sir "
{ ?_I /pres pressure [k injustice ] $value(NP) } .
:: curt

# --- attachment_loss (other-inflicted; aux = lost person) - LAMENT
" i lost $value(NP), sir "
{ ?_I /pres pressure [k attachment_loss ] $value(NP) } .

" i have carried the loss of $value(NP) ever since "
{ ?_I /pres pressure [k attachment_loss ] $value(NP) } .
:: flowery

" $value(NP) - gone "
{ ?_I /pres pressure [k attachment_loss ] $value(NP) } .
:: curt

# --- rivalry_pressure (other-inflicted; aux = rival) - GRUDGE
" $value(NP) and i, sir, we have not had a civil word in many a year "
{ ?_I /pres pressure [k rivalry_pressure ] $value(NP) } .

" there is no man i bear less love for than $value(NP) "
{ ?_I /pres pressure [k rivalry_pressure ] $value(NP) } .
:: flowery

" $value(NP) - my rival "
{ ?_I /pres pressure [k rivalry_pressure ] $value(NP) } .
:: curt


# === EMPATHIZE ==============================================================
# Speaker's emotion ABOUT the listener. v1 uses the focused-emotion belief
# shape with ?_you as the focus.

" i am sorry for you "
{ ?_I /pres emotion [k grief ] ?_you } .
" i am sorry for your loss "
{ ?_I /pres emotion [k grief ] ?_you } .
" i feel for you "
{ ?_I /pres emotion [k grief ] ?_you } .


# === OBSERVE_AFFECT =========================================================
# Inspector names the witness's apparent emotional state. Distinct from
# EMPATHIZE (which describes the speaker's own emotion); OBSERVE_AFFECT is
# observational, an invitation to elaborate. MC: TELL_FACT where the listener
# (?_you) is the subject of an emotion belief held by the speaker.

" you seem upset "
{ ?_you /pres emotion [k grief ] } .
" you seem troubled "
{ ?_you /pres emotion [k grief ] } .
" you seem afraid "
{ ?_you /pres emotion [k fear ] } .
" you seem angry "
{ ?_you /pres emotion [k anger ] } .
" you seem happy "
{ ?_you /pres emotion [k joy ] } .


# === NEGATIVE_KNOWLEDGE =====================================================
# Honest "I don't know" - distinct from DECLINE (refuses an answerable
# question) and DENY (negates a closed proposition). Uses the existing
# @unknown sentinel that every pack's Statements.mgr already authors for
# "I don't know" / "no lo sé" / "わかりません" / "ไม่ทราบ" / "Jag vet inte".
# "I don't know" itself stays in Statements.mgr; this block adds extra
# surface variants over the same MC.

" i cannot say "
@unknown
.
" i have no way of knowing "
@unknown
.
" i couldn't tell you "
@unknown
.


# === DECLINE ================================================================
# Refuses to answer an answerable question. Semantically distinct from
# NEGATIVE_KNOWLEDGE: a witness who declines COULD answer but is choosing
# not to. The receiver mind dispatches on (formulaic refusal <reason>) and
# may press, escalate, ask for the reason, or accept - all distinct from
# the response to (formulaic no_dont_know) ("I have no such belief").
#
# Reason atoms (distillation 4.2) name the witness's basis for refusal -
# the receiver mind reads them to choose its next move:
#   answer            - generic refusal of the question, no specific basis
#   speak_ill_of_dead - "nil nisi bonum" / "I'll not blacken a name"
#   religious_matter  - "between me and God"
#   above_my_station  - "such matters are above me"
#
# Vocabulary is open; new reasons added as the corpus grows. The receiver
# falls back to a generic press-for-detail when it sees a reason it does
# not yet have a specific rule for.

" i'll not say "
( formulaic refusal answer ) .
" i'd rather not say "
( formulaic refusal answer ) .
" i prefer not to discuss it "
( formulaic refusal answer ) .
" it is not fit to speak of "
( formulaic refusal answer ) .
" nil nisi bonum "
( formulaic refusal speak_ill_of_dead ) .
" i'll not blacken a name "
( formulaic refusal speak_ill_of_dead ) .
" that is between me and god "
( formulaic refusal religious_matter ) .
" such matters are above me "
( formulaic refusal above_my_station ) .
